# LeakSanitizer suppressions — ONLY one-time allocations inside third-party libraries.
# Never add our own code here: a leak in src/ must be fixed, not suppressed.
#
# Usage:  LSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/lsan.supp" ctest --test-dir build-asan
#
# libproxy: unless a socket is told otherwise, Qt Network asks libproxy for the system
# proxy once per process, and libproxy keeps ~141 bytes for the life of the process.
# Our publisher and receiver use QNetworkProxy::NoProxy, but the tests also use plain
# QTcpSocket clients (standing in for any third-party client), which trigger it.
leak:libpxbackend-1.0.so
leak:libproxy.so.1
